Local trophies in the sceNpTrophy HLE. CreateContext reads the title's TROPHY.TRP ($PS3_TROPHY_TRP, else an installed
update's <hdd0>/game/<title>/TROPDIR/<commId>/, else <vfs root>/PS3_GAME/TROPDIR/<commId>/): ids, grades, hidden flags,
platinum links (pid), names and details from TROP.SFM (TROPCONF.SFM if absent). The trophy count is the set's (KZ3 1.14:
79, disc: 52) instead of the fixed 128; a missing or unreadable TRP is logged and leaves 128 anonymous slots while
Init/CreateContext/CreateHandle/RegisterContext still return CELL_OK (KZ3's trophycheck.gum blocks on any error there).
UnlockTrophy refuses the platinum itself (PLATINUM_CANNOT_UNLOCK), and when the unlock completes every trophy whose pid
names the platinum it unlocks the platinum too and writes its id to *platinumId (else -1). The store moves from the
cwd-relative gamedata/trophies/<commId>.json to <hdd0>/home/<user>/trophy/<commId>/TROPUSR.json (hdd0 = $PS3_HDD0_ROOT,
else <vfs root>/dev_hdd0 if present, else gamedata/dev_hdd0), written to a temp file and renamed; the old file is
migrated once; SetStoragePath keeps the old flat layout. GetGameInfo/GetTrophyInfo use the TRP and now write their
u32/u64 fields big-endian; GetRequiredDiskSpace answers the TRP size; AbortHandle is added. Host API:
ps3_trophy_set_notify(fn, user) is called per unlock (then once for the platinum) with comm id, id, grade, hidden, name,
detail, for a host toast; ps3_trophy_set_user(id). Test: tools/assets/test_trophy5004.sh (host harness, real TRPs read
in the sandbox, negative control against the unpatched file). Upstream candidate (platinum, count, store path, BE
structs).

